BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pasta Machine Printing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T160000
UID:260728LbcHxsDJ1k2C5H37DcEDcg
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, August 1\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 4:00 PM\n\nLocation
 \n\nRoom 208\n\nCategory\n\nPrintmaking\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\
 n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$110\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\
 n$25\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$135\n\nJoin guest Bay Area artist\, B
 ettina Pauly in a special one-day workshop in learning how to use differen
 t materials to create a printmaking plate for a pasta machine using water 
 soluble etching inks. Create your own prints using a pasta machine as a pr
 ess!Learn how to revive your manual hand crank pasta maker to make small d
 rypoint fine line prints. This popular technique uses the pressure that n
 ormally rolls out pasta dough to print artwork instead! Students will enga
 ge with milk cartons\, Tetra Paks\, and Akua plate material. Learn how to 
 properly ink up the plate\, add packing to the pasta maker for the perfect
  impression\, and pull prints to make a small format 4 x 6 edition that ca
 n be produced multiple times. The instructor will demonstrate how easy it 
 is to use and clean a pasta machine so using it for pasta AND printing can
  be an option. Prints will be made using a drypoint needle and a cutting k
 nife\, and will be printed on Rives BFK paper with oil-based etching inks.
  This will be a day of fun experimentation in printmaking!The materials fe
 e includes\; drypoint needle\, chipboard\, felt and printing papers that s
 tudents will be able to take home to continue making prints on their own p
 asta machines. Please note: This class requires some hand dexterity to ma
 neuver the etching tools and pasta machine. Participants should feel comfo
 rtable using tools with sharp edges.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/pasta-machine-printing/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Unity Garden Rock Painting Party
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T160000
UID:260728AzF8CrYgoEOu2dxTc5eK6A
DESCRIPTION:The Vallejo Project is inviting families\, neighbors\, artists
 \, and community supporters to join a fun-filled afternoon celebrating cre
 ativity\, community\, and the Unity Garden during its Rock Painting Party 
 on SATURDAY August 1ST\, 2026\, from 1:00 p.m. to 4:00 p.m. at 2160 Sacram
 ento Street\, Vallejo\, CA.The free community event will bring people toge
 ther to paint colorful rocks that will become part of the Unity Garden\, c
 reating a lasting symbol of hope\, resilience\, and community pride. Parti
 cipants of all ages are welcome\, and no artistic experience is necessary.
 \n\nIn addition to rock painting\, guests can enjoy\, fresh homemade lemon
 ade\, a tomato sauce-making demonstration\, Opportunities to sign up for u
 pcoming Vallejo Project programs\, volunteer registration and family-frien
 dly activities celebrating creativity and community connection.\n\nThe Uni
 ty Garden serves as a gathering place where residents learn about healthy 
 living\, food production\, environmental stewardship\, and neighborhood en
 gagement. The Rock Painting Party is designed to help commemorate the gard
 en while welcoming new volunteers and supporters into the Vallejo Project 
 community.
LOCATION:Unity Garden
URL:https://www.vallejoproject.org/events
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Outlet Gallery & Block Party 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T200000
UID:2607285cgfbnUSOEax5_nPpLijqg
DESCRIPTION:The Outlet Gallery Art\, Healing\, and Community with First Re
 sponders Saturday\, August 1 | 3-8 PM Mare Island Brewing Co. - Coal Shed 
 Brewery | Vallejo\, CA Free admission. Firefighters and first responders c
 arry experiences most people never see. For many\, art becomes the outlet.
  The Outlet is a free art show hosted by First Responders Outlet\, a nonpr
 ofit founded by firefighters from the Richmond Fire Department. This event
  brings original artwork\, live music\, and community together along the V
 allejo waterfront - and opens a window into the creative lives of the peop
 le who serve us. Original artwork created by first responders Food trucks 
 Resource tents and vendors Interactive art experiences Dedicated kid zones
  Silent auction and raffles Live music Craft beer\, wine\, and cocktails  
 Learn more about The Outlet on their website and Instagram.   View this pr
 ofile on Instagram     The Outlet \\(@ the\\_outlet\\_first\\_responders\\
 ) - Instagram photos and videos
