BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tails & Trails at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T110000
UID:260722Sem74Cchf026AMErEHFpwg
DESCRIPTION:Jack London’s lifelong admiration for dogs was inspired by h
 is experiences in the Klondike and immortalized in “The Call of the Wild
 ” and “White Fang.” His unforgettable canine characters remind us of
  the loyalty\, courage\, and companionship that dogs bring to our lives\, 
 making this park the perfect place to honor our own furry companions.\n\nI
 n celebration of National Dog Month\, a group of up to 15 dogs and their p
 eople will take a relaxed\, three-mile guided walk through London’s hist
 oric Beauty Ranch to the Wolf House ruins.\n\nAlong the way\, there will b
 e fascinating stories about the park’s history\, and plenty of opportuni
 ties to sniff\, explore\, and take in the sights together.  This leisurel
 y\, community-focused walk includes water breaks\, treat stops\, and time 
 to connect with fellow dog lovers.\n\nJack London State Historic Park is a
  wildlife sanctuary\, therefore dogs are only allowed in designated histor
 ic areas including the Beauty Ranch area and on the trail to Wolf House bu
 t not on any other trails.  For more information about dogs at Jack Londo
 n State Historic Park\, visit https://jacklondonpark.com/policies/.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/tails-and-trails-august-2026-copy/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Community Wellness Fair hosted by Community Market and community p
 artners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T170000
UID:260722EriEXLnV80--_AG14_ZRlQ
DESCRIPTION:Join Community Market at our annual Community Wellness Fair fo
 r a full day of wellness\, learning\, self-care\, and community connection
 .\n\nThis year’s fair brings together local practitioners\, educators\, 
 makers\, and wellness-focused businesses for a day centered around care\, 
 discovery\, and well-being. Guests will have the opportunity to explore a 
 wide range of offerings\, including one-on-one wellness services\, educati
 onal speakers\, local vendors\, a curated wellness boutique\, food\, drink
 s\, and more.\n\nThe Community Wellness Fair is a chance to connect with l
 ocal wellness providers\, learn about different approaches to health and w
 ell-being\, discover new resources\, and spend time in community. Whether 
 you are looking for support\, inspiration\, education\, or simply a meanin
 gful way to spend the day\, the fair offers something for anyone intereste
 d in wellness and self-care.\n\nAttendees can browse vendor booths\, meet 
 practitioners\, enjoy wellness services\, listen to speakers\, shop though
 tfully selected products\, and learn more about the people and organizatio
 ns offering wellness resources in our community.\n\nMore details about par
 ticipating vendors\, services\, speakers\, and offerings will be shared so
 on.\n\nEvent Details Saturday\, August 1 11 AM to 5 PM SEB Arts 282 S. Hig
 h Street\, Sebastopol\, CA\n\nTickets Advance tickets are $10 through July
  27. Tickets will be $15 at the door.\n\nFor more information or to purcha
 se tickets\, visit cmnaturalfoods.com/cwf-tickets
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center For the Arts
URL:https://www.cmnaturalfoods.com/cwf-tickets
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nature Hike Vallejo Swett Ranches
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T130000
UID:260721fXD_ZgeeMESoc9Uz7acpWQ
DESCRIPTION:Come explore the hills between Fairfield\, Benicia\, and Valle
 jo. Solano Land Trust docents will guide you through this area\, known as 
 the King-Swett Ranches. Docents will share insights about the birds and ot
 her wildlife that call this area home\, and give you a great workout!\n\nH
 ike level: Moderate to Moderately Strenuous Please note: Vallejo Swett is 
 an undeveloped property with no formal trails. This is a rugged & an off t
 rail hike. Participants could be climbing or going under fences\, and tree
  branches. Docents also can go up & along of steep and clumpy ground mount
 ain sides.\n\n\\*Please note\, cancellation of the hike may occur due to C
 ounty Fire Danger Warnings and closures of open spaces and parks. Once reg
 istered\, you will receive any updates should this ever happen.
LOCATION:Vallejo Swett Ranches
URL:https://solanolandtrust.org/events-news/event-calendar.html/event/2026
 /08/01/nature-hike-at-vallejo-swett-ranches-august-/566217
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
