BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Right to Thrive: Tenant-Led Housing Justice in Vallejo
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T150000
UID:260728jWS-FhwLUUuWDovh8BIt9A
DESCRIPTION:El 1 de agosto\, inquilinas/os de Vallejo\, organizadoras/es y
  liderazgos comunitarios se reunirán para el lanzamiento comunitario de E
 l Derecho a Prosperar \, y para impulsar las protecciones fuertes que nues
 tras familias necesitan. Este es un momento para unirse\, compartir la ver
 dad y fortalecer nuestro poder colectivo.\n\nThe Vallejo Housing Justice C
 oalition along with Supervisor Cassandra James and End Poverty in Californ
 ia\, Public Advocates\, and Urban Habitat will co‑host the release of Th
 e Right to Thrive: Tenant‑Led Housing Justice in Vallejo\, California. T
 he briefing will feature key voices and findings from the report’s tenan
 t‑led research\,illuminating the dire housing conditions Vallejo familie
 s are navigating and the urgent need for strong tenant protections.\n\nAut
 hored by Aneteeniya Bell\, The Right to Thrive was developed in partnershi
 p with Urban Habitat - where VHJC was originally incubated - and received 
 major editorial support from Chris Schildt\, the organization’s Director
  of Housing Justice.\n\nVallejo renters are facing a housing emergency of 
 rising rents\, unstable housing conditions\, and mounting displacement pre
 ssures. The Right to Thrive draws on tenant‑led research and firsthand t
 estimony to document how these conditions affect the health\, stability\, 
 and future of Vallejo’s residents and neighborhoods.\n\nMost people want
  their neighbors to have access to the housing they need—but the systems
  in place today aren’t fair for everyone. The report points to the unjus
 t barriers standing in the way and argues that replacing them with communi
 ty-led\, democratic solutions is a matter of fairness and dignity that mak
 es Vallejo better for everyone.\n\nThe briefing will outline why local ten
 ant protections are urgently needed and how community‑led solutions can 
 strengthen Vallejo’s housing landscape. The “Right to Thrive” briefi
 ng will include remarks from the co‑hosts\, a presentation of the report
 ’s key findings\, and tenant testimony.
LOCATION:Vallejo Naval and Historical Museum
URL:https://www.facebook.com/VallejoHousingJusticeCoalition/posts/pfbid033
 Yave3keGGcJfT9B5oLdFVMCb8FUWyFw3gT2YpZbBr9XfRDTmN8XgtnQjQ3VLN9sl
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
