DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260802T170000
UID:260728ouNfnqo1xUCatzJSOeLCCA
DESCRIPTION:Bank of America cardholders receive free general admission to 
 participating museums nationwide on the first full weekend of each month\;
  this month is August 1-2. \n\nLooking for a chance to squeeze the last d
 rop out of summer and beat the heat? The Sonoma Valley Museum of Art has e
 xciting exhibits including John Paul Morabito: Dancing in the Night\, feat
 uring colorful weaving\, and Norma I. Quintana: Paradise of Memory / Para
 íso de la Memoria\, a portrait series linking memory with community ident
 ity. Inspired by portraits created by itinerant photographers in Puerto Ri
 co\, her images honor everyday lives as a vital part of cultural remembran
 ce. These “jewels of memory” capture not just faces\, but also the tra
 ces of experience that bind people across generations.\n\nBank of America 
 Museums on Us program offers FREE weekend general admission on the first f
 ull weekend of every month to Bank of America\, Merrill and Bank of Americ
 a Private Bank credit and debit cardholders. All you need is your Bank of 
 America\, Merrill\, or Bank of America Private Bank card and picture ID fo
 r access. \n\nAdditional participating museums can be found here: https:/
 /about.bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-partner
LOCATION:Sonoma Valle Museum of Art
URL:https://about.bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-part
 ners
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Overeaters Anonymous (OA) Meeting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260802T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260802T103000
UID:260728cDsjNvivwUKCxcc-s6_9aQ
DESCRIPTION:Is Food a Problem for You? You Are Not Alone.\n\nIn OA\, membe
 rs experience spiritual\, emotional\, and physical recovery by practicing 
 the Twelve Steps and living by their spiritual principles—one day at a t
 ime.\n\nOvereaters Anonymous \\(OA\\) is a fellowship of people who suppor
 t each other in recovering from compulsive eating and food behaviors. If y
 ou feel you have a problem with food\, OA welcomes you—no matter what yo
 ur background\, beliefs\, or eating habits. \n\nWe hold an in-person meet
 ings at 9:30 on Sunday mornings at Church of the Nazarene\, 18980 Arnold D
 rive\, Sonoma\, CA \\(a small room directly off of parking lot\; look for 
 the sign posted\\) and newcomers are always welcome.\n\nYou may view all N
 orth Bay OA in-person and online meetings at https://www.northbayoa.org/me
 etings.html\n\nOA is not a diet club or calorie-counting program.\n\nMembe
 rs have different plans of eating.\n\nOA does not endorse any specific foo
 d plan. \n\nVisit: https://www.northbayoa.org/\n\nFind a meeting: https:/
 /www.northbayoa.org/meetings.html
URL:https://www.northbayoa.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
