BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:First Christian Church of Vallejo Community Picnic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260804T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260804T173000
UID:260728xJVRsOlvS0O-FE3CDEZiRg
DESCRIPTION:First Christian Church \\(FCC\\) of Vallejo extends a warm inv
 itation to attend a free Community Picnic on Tuesday\, Aug 04\, 2026\, sta
 rting at 5:30 PM. Held on the church grounds at 1035 Indiana St.\, the eve
 ning promises a vibrant gathering filled with fellowship\, food\, ice crea
 m\, music\, and fun.\n\nA central highlight of the event will be the offic
 ial dedication of the church’s newly installed public water bottle refil
 l station.\n\nThe project was launched in the fall of 2025 when FCC Vallej
 o was awarded a $6\,000 Mission and Ministry Grant from the Christian Chur
 ch \\(Disciples of Christ\\) National Benevolent Association \\(NBA\\). Gu
 ided by a deep commitment to environmental care\, the congregation sought 
 a sustainable alternative to distributing single-use bottled water to visi
 tors\, leveraging the grant to better align their daily outreach with valu
 es of living lightly on the earth.\n\nPermanently installed in front of th
 e church alongside the community's existing Little Free Pantry\, the stati
 on was completed using a mix of commercial expertise and volunteer labor o
 n Earth Sunday in April 2026. It has already become a vital neighborhood r
 esource\, actively utilized by local residents\, building occupants\, unsh
 eltered guests\, workers\, students\, and passersby alike.\n\n"We hope the
  community can join us to celebrate this wonderful addition to the neighbo
 rhood\," the church shared in a statement. "Bring your favorite reusable w
 ater bottle and take part in this dedication!"\n\nFirst Christian Church o
 f Vallejo holds a rich 126-year history of inclusive\, community-focused m
 inistry. Situated in a diverse West Vallejo neighborhood near residential 
 areas\, commercial spaces\, schools\, and fellow congregations\, the churc
 h serves as a hub for both local and global outreach. Notable efforts incl
 ude a long-standing partnership with Sustainable Solano to manage a demons
 tration community garden that supplies fresh produce to Faith Food Fridays
  and the Amador Street Hope Center. The campus also hosts a meditative pea
 ce garden\, a Little Free Pantry\, more than 10 weekly self-help recovery 
 groups\, and partners semi-annually with Vallejo Together and Lighthouse F
 ellowship Church to provide free haircuts and hot showers to neighbors exp
 eriencing need.\n\nFree admission\; attendees are encouraged to bring thei
 r own reusable water bottles.
LOCATION:First Christian Church of Vallejo
URL:https://vallejochristian.org/news-%26-events
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
