BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Plein Air Tree Drawing in Mixed Media at Jack London State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T140000
UID:260627oPuWOdGdoU2oU4PaHaIQhQ
DESCRIPTION:Date & Time\n\nSaturday\, July 11\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 2:00 
 PM\n\nEvent Series\n\nView all classes in this series here.\n\nLocation\n\
 nJack London State Historical Park\n\nCategory\n\nDrawing & Painting\, Wor
 kshops\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegist
 ration Cost:\n\n$75\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$5\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\
 n$80\n\nIn this one-day workshop\, participants will learn and practice fo
 undational drawing techniques while sketching the beautiful trees at Jack 
 London State Park. Each student will choose a tree to draw\, and then spen
 d time rendering their subject while receiving instruction in proportion a
 nd other key drawing skills.Once students have an established drawing\, th
 ey will explore the light and shadow on their tree with inventive colors i
 n watercolor. Practice and build your observational drawing skills\, spend
  time in nature\, and have fun with color!Discover the meditative benefits
  of a plein air art practice\, and gain a deeper appreciation for the natu
 ral world around you through close observation and intentional rendering. 
 No prior drawing experience necessary\; beginners welcome. All materials a
 re provided and all experience and skill levels are welcome!After the work
 shop you may choose to go hiking\, tour the museum\, or walk to the ruins 
 of the Wolf House.Important note: There is a Vehicle Entry Fee of $15. Aft
 er the kiosk\, veer to the right and proceed to the parking lot. All stude
 nts will meet the instructor in the parking lot and walk together to the w
 orkshop area. Dress for the weather and bring a water bottle and snacks or
  a bag lunch.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/plein-air-tree-drawing-july
 -2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Story Shuffle: The Truth\, The Half Truth and Nothing Like The
  Truth!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T210000
UID:260626BJ_9XwQvC0m8e6gvUzfrOg
DESCRIPTION:The Story Shuffle - The Truth\, The Half Truth and Nothing Lik
 e The Truth!\n\nJoin us for storytelling in Novato! We’ll have two to th
 ree featured storytellers and then an Open Mic part of the show\, featurin
 g two options: you can either throw your name in the hat to tell a 5-minut
 e story or a 1-minute story in our Story Sprint lighting round. No theme\,
  just bring your best story. Sign up at the door. Come out for a night of 
 live\, friendly and fun storytelling in a cozy\, comfortable venue that is
  just right for an evening of great tales. We’d love to see you there!
LOCATION:Courtyard by Marriott
URL:http://sfapshows.com/shuffle.php
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Imaginists present: BEACHED
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T213000
UID:260625PDPk6oYrHkGaCtj_4KaM7g
DESCRIPTION:A new play by G.B. Lindsay.\n\nOld friends\, Jaycoen (Stephen 
 K Patterson) and Ougein (GB Lindsay) wake up to another delightful day at 
 the beach as ocean sings and war rages on. But Today enters like no other 
 Yesterday\, for this day has arrived with new twisted turns and burns\, tu
 cked-up into its sun-worn sleeves. Enter six extraordinary beings (mostly 
 Taylor Diffenderfer) who will test the limits of their friendship and the 
 inevitability of their fate.\n\nBeached is an absurdist tragicomedy in the
  tradition of Laurel and Hardy\, Beckett\, Kafka\, Tom Stoppard\, and Eric
  Overmyer.
LOCATION:The Imaginists
URL:https://theimaginists.org/beached-julyaug
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
