BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cookbook Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T133000
UID:260722UgCa1mCvGkm7cwRw7AeDOA
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in trying new recipes or just wanting to ge
 t out of your cooking comfort zone? A cookbook book club blends the joy of
  reading with the creativity of cooking and the warmth of sharing meals. B
 rowse a selection of themed cookbooks every month\, then prepare and share
  your meals for the next meeting! June: Celebrating Julia in June! Julia C
 hild & Those Influenced by Her. Before "food TV" was a genre\, Julia Child
  was teaching America to cook-joyfully\, loudly\, and with plenty of permi
 ssion to make mistakes. Her landmark cookbook Mastering the Art of French 
 Cooking helped translate French technique for American home kitchens launc
 hing a whole new way of learning to cook. For this meeting\, bring a dish 
 by Julia Child or by chefs influenced by her and who share her spirit-like
  Jacques Pépin\, her longtime cooking partner on public television\, and 
 Ina Garten\, who has spoken about admiring Child's "courage of her convict
 ions." July: Savoring Summer\, Italian-Style. Think Italian summer at its 
 best: farmers' market produce\, quick meals that beat the heat\, and bold\
 , clean flavors. Expect inspiration from light pastas\, crisp salads\, gri
 lled vegetables\, and fruit-forward desserts-everything that tastes like s
 unshine. Plates\, cutlery\, and refreshments provided. Please be aware tha
 t dishes may contain or come into contact with common allergens\, such as 
 dairy\, eggs\, wheat\, soybeans\, tree nuts\, peanuts\, fish\, or shellfis
 h. If you are interested in attending please contact Kate at Sonoma Valley
  Library for more information. \\(707\\) 996-5217 kdeadder@sonomalibrary.o
 rg
LOCATION:Sonoma Valley Regional Library
URL:https://events.sonomalibrary.org/event/cookbook-club-103268
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
