BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Marin Farmers Markets
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260813T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260813T130000
UID:260728HGbyHTt1qEeACxHhhHfCiw
DESCRIPTION:Price: Free\n\nSponsor: Marin Center\n\nExplore the bounty of 
 summer at the Marin Farmers Markets. Taste vine-ripened tomatoes\, corn th
 at was picked that morning\, and peaches so juicy you have to bend over ju
 st to get a bite. Farm-fresh eggs\, grass-fed beef\, artisan c heeses\, ra
 w milk\, and freshly baked breads complete the shopping exper ience. Speci
 alty prepared foods and handmade art add to the magic of the market.\n\nEn
 joy the intimate feeling of the Thursday Marin Farmers Market\, an ideal p
 lace to meet for lunch and pick up fresh produce for the weekend. Discover
  the abundance and diversity of product at the celebrated Sunday Marin Far
 mers Market\, the third largest farmers market in California. Turn your do
 llar into a vote for local sustainable agriculture\, shrink your eco-footp
 rint\, and revive the feeling of being intimate ly connected to your food 
 by meeting your farmers face-to-face. The market takes place rain or shine
 .\n\nwww.aginstitutemarin.org
LOCATION:Marin Veterans' Memorial Auditorium
URL:https://www.marincounty.gov/county-marin-calendar
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:No Place To Grow Old: Film Screening & Panel Discussion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260813T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260813T200000
UID:2607282Snraz82xUiAtCyv1DYlWA
DESCRIPTION:On Thursday\, August 13\, join the San Geronimo Valley Commun
 ity Center\, Two Valleys Community Land Trust and Marin AgeWell Collaborat
 ive for a free special screening of No Place to Grow Old\, a thought-prov
 oking documentary that explores the growing challenges older adults face i
 n finding safe\, affordable housing and maintaining dignity as they age. T
 hrough personal stories and expert perspectives\, the film examines the co
 mplex realities of aging\, housing insecurity\, and the importance of comm
 unity support. Following the screening\, a panel of local advocates and pr
 ofessionals will lead a discussion on how these issues are affecting older
  adults in Marin County and the ways our community can work together to cr
 eate more inclusive\, age-friendly solutions. Audience members will be inv
 ited to participate in the conversation and share their own questions and 
 perspectives.
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Communiy Center
URL:https://sgvperformingarts.eventcalendarapp.com/no-place-to-grow-old-fi
 lm-screening-and-panel-discussion-1
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
