BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Park Rx—Beginner Hiking for Fitness
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T130000
UID:260701hXYdvF-9W0apv0nVTEZpXw
DESCRIPTION:Join us on this fitness program\, where the leaders w
 ill guide you on a series of 8 weekly hikes with the challenge
  increasing each week. Before the first hike\, the leader will 
 discuss proper shoes\, hydration\, incorporating hiking poles\, pro
 per pacing\, etc. The group's final hike aims for the long rout
 e up Brushy Peaks Trail\, where hikers can enjoy the beautiful 
 vistas.\n\nThe following is a list of possible routes selected fo
 r this hiking series: 1) Sat 8/1 - White Barn to Uranus\, 2.1 
 miles\, 180 ft elev \\[meet @ white barn\\] 2) Sat 8/8 - Meadow
 - Hillside loop\, 3 miles\, 490 ft elev \\[meet @ white barn\\]
  3) Sat 8/15 - Lake Ralphine & Spring Lake loop\, 4.3 miles\, 
 420 ft elev \\[meet @ Howarth Park's Boathouse\\] 4) Sat 8/22- J
 ack London State Historic Park\, May’s Clearing\, 3.5 miles\, 8
 20 ft elev \\[meet @ upper parking lot\, 2400 London Ranch Road
 \, Glen Ellen\, CA 95442\\] 5) Sat 8/29 - Vista Trail loop\, 3.
 5 miles\, 830 ft elev \\[meet @ white barn\\] 6) Sat 9/5 – S
 tern + Waterfall loop\, 2.7 miles\, 750 ft elev \\[meet @ main
  lot\\] 7) Sat 9/12 – Sonoma Valley Regional Park & Lake Sutt
 onfield loop\, 4.3\, miles\, 770 ft elev \\[meet at Valley of t
 he Moon Trailhead on Arnold Dr.\\] 8) Sat 9/19 – Hillside to 
 Neptune picnic table\, 4.4 miles\, 970 ft elev \\[meet @ white 
 barn\\]\n\nPlease note these routes or dates are subject to chang
 e depending on logistics. Wear appropriate footwear for rocky/slip
 pery trails and layers. Bring at least a quart (32oz) of water\
 , and if desired\, a snack. The group will be limited to 35 p
 articipants.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/beghffsummer26
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing at Lynmar Estate
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T143000
UID:260626bTSUf6ylYkCgw1XenfPYQA
DESCRIPTION:Rooted in the bounty of Quail Hill Vineyard\, Lynmar Estate’
 s Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing invites guests to experience the flavors
  of Sonoma County at their seasonal peak. The elevated four-course menu sh
 owcases ingredients harvested from Lynmar’s organically farmed gardens\,
  orchards\, and olive groves. Each course is individually plated and thoug
 htfully paired with Lynmar’s acclaimed estate-grown Pinot Noirs\, Chardo
 nnays\, and sparkling wines\, creating a journey that is both deeply conne
 cted to Sonoma County and globally inspired. Served in the idyllic setting
  of Quail Hill Vineyard\, the experience is further enhanced by a special 
 tableside visit from Estate Chef David Frakes.\n\nCollectors Lunch Pairing
  Menu Summer 2026:\n\nAdam’s Vineyard Chardonnay\, 2022\n\nWarm Organic 
 Popcorn\n\nWhite Corn-Kasundi Salt\, Estate Extra-Virgin Olive Oil\n\nSusa
 nna’s Vineyard Chardonnay\, 2022\n\nThai Green Curry & Coconut Soup\n\nB
 liss Snap Peas & Heirloom Radish\n\nYoung Vines Pinot Noir\, 2021\n\nHeirl
 oom Potato & Cherry Tomato ‘Croustade’\n\nSmoked Bacon-Grain Mustard D
 ressing\n\nSusanna’s Vineyard Pinot Noir\, 2022\n\nRoasted Syrian Seven-
 Spiced Chicken Breast\n\nIndonesian Corn Fritter\, Summer Vegetable Ragout
 \, Balado Sauce\n\nRosé de Blancs Sparkling\, 2021\n\nChilled Vanilla Bur
 nt Basque Cheesecake\n\nRaspberry-Rose Syrup\, Black Tea & Licorice-Poache
 d Cherries\n\nBrown Butter Nilla Cookie\, Candied Lime\n\nEstate Ingredien
 ts:\n\nBay Laurel\, Cherries\, Chives\, Edible Flowers\, Lemons\, Olive Oi
 l\, Peas\, Potatoes\, Radishes\, Raspberries\, Thyme\, Tomatoes\, Zucchini
  and more!\n\nMenu by Estate Chef David Frakes\n\nReservations are require
 d. Maximum group size is six guests.
LOCATION:Lynmar Estate
URL:https://lynmarestate.com/reservation/type/collectors-lunch-pairing/ 
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
