BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Roots & Resonance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T130000
UID:2607205DRoAJyO_UeGuEPS4V5ivw
DESCRIPTION:Hannah Mayree \\(they/them\\) is an artist and musician whose 
 work as a banjoist\, multi-instrumentalist\, producer and vocalist has bee
 n a historic excavation of folk music as well as a window into the future 
 of folk. Hannah has a body of work that highlights original and traditiona
 l banjo compositions as well as harmonies through acoustic live vocal loop
 ing and involves audiences in community singing.  On the dawn of releasing
  their second studio album following the 2017\, Thoughts of the Night\, Ha
 nnah's evolution as a musician has included holding down solo performances
  as well as duo\, trio and full band configurations and highlights both th
 e Black string and tradition as well as innovating between genres\, expres
 sing the conditions of our world and sparking change through culturally st
 ewarded experiences they curate for music loving communities.  They founde
 d and creatively direct the Black Banjo Reclamation Project which is curre
 ntly creating musical\, cultural and land-based opportunities for Black\, 
 Afro-Diasporic communities around the world to work with the banjo as a to
 ol for reclaiming ancestral wisdom & creating Afro-futures. Follow her on 
 social media! https://www.instagram.com/hannah\\_mayree/?hl=en https://www
 .facebook.com/hannahmayree/ https://hannahmayree.bandcamp.com/album/though
 ts-of-the-night https://www.bandsintown.com/a/13525249-hannah-mayree?came\
 \_from=250&utm\\_medium=web&utm\\_source=artist\\_event\\_page&utm\\_campa
 ign=lineup\\_artist https://www.blackbanjoreclamationproject.org
LOCATION:Vallejo John F. Kennedy Library
URL:https://solanolibrary.libnet.info/event/16433101
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
