SUMMARY:Cotati Accordion Festival at La Plaza Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260816T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260816T000000
UID:260616UACJysKwBU6Yz7-B-wC1ag
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate music\, culture\, and community at the two-day Cotat
 i Accordion Festival. This lively\, family-friendly event features five st
 ages showcasing everything from zydeco\, polka\, and cumbia to jazz\, rock
 \, Balkan\, classical\, and more. Guests can enjoy a dedicated polka tent\
 , a two-day zydeco dance party\, jam sessions\, and performances from musi
 cians around the world. Families will find plenty to enjoy\, including a l
 arge playground\, wildlife exhibits\, a children's area\, face painting\, 
 food vendors\, and artisan booths. Kids 15 and under receive free admissio
 n\, and free parking with shuttle service is available. Beer and wine will
  be available for purchase. Visit the event website for performance schedu
 les and event hours.
LOCATION:La Plaza Park
URL:https://www.sonoma.com/event/cotati-accordion-festival-at-la-plaza-par
 k/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:I Need a Mic: Open Mic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260816T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260816T140000
UID:260725rkd2QuICdEGU8aZtQNgZ5w
DESCRIPTION:Welcome poets\, writers\, and artists of Vallejo. My name is R
 ay\, and I am your host of I NEED A MIC OPEN MIC.\n\nThis is more than jus
 t a stage — it’s a space. A space where voices rise\, stories breathe\
 , and truth finds its rhythm. \n\nWhether you carry poems in your chest\,
  songs in your spirit\, or stories that have been waiting for the right mo
 ment — this is your invitation.\n\nWe gather not just to perform\, but t
 o connect. To celebrate the raw\, the real\, and the unapologetically huma
 n art of expression. Every voice matters here. Every perspective adds to t
 he pulse of this room.\n\nBut understand — this is a space built on resp
 ect. While we welcome passion\, depth\, and honesty\, we do not tolerate h
 ate\, disrespect\, or harmful rhetoric. Heavy political agendas that divid
 e rather than inspire have no place here. \n\nThis stage is for expressio
 n\, not oppression.\n\nBring your truth. Bring your courage. Bring your ar
 t.\n\nCome share. Come listen. Come feel something.\n\nBecause someone in 
 that room might need exactly what you have to say.\n\nI NEED A MIC — and
  maybe\, so do you.\n\nListen to the I Need a Mic Podcast here\, or on you
 r favorite podcast platform: https://open.spotify.com/show/5cPncyZy3AP82vP
 pxEx2LH
LOCATION:City Arts Gallery
URL:https://linktr.ee/INeedAMic
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Broadway Under the Stars - Mamma Mia!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260816T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260816T220000
UID:260517IviYGPOulEiAt2voHU7HRg
DESCRIPTION:The global smash hit is coming to Sonoma for the very first ti
 me! Set on a sun-drenched Greek island\, *Mamma Mia!* follows a young br
 ide-to-be on a quest to discover the identity of her father — bringing t
 hree very unexpected guests from her mother’s past back into their lives
 . Fueled by ABBA’s greatest hits (including “Dancing Queen\,” “Ma
 mma Mia\,” “The Winner Takes It All\,” and more)\, this joyful tale 
 of family\, friendship\, love\, and second chances has captured the hearts
  of millions worldwide. With its large cast\, explosive dance numbers\, no
 nstop humor\, and irresistible score\, *Mamma Mia!* promises to be one o
 f the biggest and most unforgettable productions in Transcendence history.
 \n\n*Mamma Mia!* is presented through special arrangement with Music Thea
 tre International (MTI). All authorized performance materials are also sup
 plied by MTI. www.mtishows.com
LOCATION:Sonoma Field of Dreams
URL:https://transcendencetheatre.org/whats-on/mamma-mia/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Trombone Shorty & Orleans Avenue and St. Paul & the Broken Bones
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260816T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260816T190000
UID:260722OUUZHz3amU6Ki0iZolCTDg
DESCRIPTION:Trombone Shorty & Orleans Avenue and St. Paul & the Broken Bon
 es with special guest Tré Burt Sun\, August 16\, 2026 at 7 pm. Weill Hall
  \\+ Lawn Few artists embody the heart and soul of their city like Trombon
 e Shorty. Perhaps the most recognizable ambassador for New Orleans music w
 orking today\, Shorty has spent his entire life not only carrying the torc
 h for Crescent City culture\, but also propelling it forward into the 21st
  century with his ecstatic live performances and intoxicating blend of roc
 k\, funk\, soul\, jazz\, blues\, hip-hop\, and Caribbean influences. Born 
 Troy Andrews\, Shorty made his first appearance at New Orleans’ iconic J
 azz Fest at the age of four\, when he took the stage for an impromptu perf
 ormance with Bo Diddley. By six\, he was heading up his own brass band\, a
 nd by his early twenties\, he’d released the first in a string of critic
 ally acclaimed\, chart-topping albums that would lead to performances ever
 ywhere from the White House and the Grammy Awards to Madison Square Garden
  and the 2025 Super Bowl. St. Paul & The Broken Bones are a powerhouse sou
 l ensemble from Alabama known for their electrifying live shows and impass
 ioned vocals. Formed in Birmingham in 2011\, the band features Paul Janewa
 y \\(vocals\\)\, Jesse Phillips \\(bass\\)\, Browan Lollar \\(guitar\\)\, 
 Kevin Leon \\(drums\\)\, Al Gamble \\(keyboards\\)\, Allen Branstetter \\(
 trumpet\\)\, Chad Fisher \\(trombone\\)\, and Amari Ansari \\(saxophone\\)
 .  Their new self-titled sixth album marks a creative renewal—melding th
 e band’s adventurous spirit with a return to soulful\, song-focused root
 s. Recorded at the legendary FAME Studios and produced by Eg White \\(Adel
 e\, Celine Dion\\)\, the record blends psych-funk grooves\, gospel-tinged 
 ballads\, and cinematic rock flourishes. Tracks like “Sushi and Coca-Col
 a” and “Going Back” reflect both personal introspection and the band
 ’s deepened identity after a decade of evolution.
LOCATION:Green Music Center
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1175808641098293/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
