BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Amina Figarova Edition 113
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260816T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260816T210000
UID:260715NPtFKs_nnE6OiYi8UFczgA
DESCRIPTION:Pianist and composer Amina Figarova leads her ensemble Edition
  113 in an acoustic performance that highlights the group's interplay\, cl
 arity of sound\, and expressive range within a chamber jazz setting. "I lo
 ve the energy and the feel of the city." Azerbaijani-born Amina Figarova s
 ettled in Harlem in 2014. Edition 113 is named for the city block where sh
 e and Belgian-born flautist Bart Platteau live. After 20 years of touring 
 her acoustic band\, the new recording seems to celebrate New York with a m
 ix of modern jazz\, funk - and Figarova's distinctive\, thoughtful writing
 .Other band members include Rez Abbasi on guitar\, Amina Scott on bass and
  Ferenc Nemeth on drums. Aptly titled\, Persistenceis a surprising delight
  and one that seemingly avoids many of the pitfalls of fusion. The opening
  title track launches into enthralling rhythmic interplay between drums an
 d bass\, while flutist Bart Platteau channels the spirit of the Headhunter
 s in his soaring melodies. Figarova\, meanwhile\, artfully comps\, switchi
 ng between piano and synthesizer. The record continues in this breathless 
 vein\, riffing off of Robert Glasper's hip-hop mentality for "I've Got No 
 Time\," while "R Song" highlights Platteau and Figarova's almost telepathi
 c interweaving with guitarist Rez Abbasi. Even on slower numbers - "Mornin
 g Blue" and "Horizons"-Figarova and her band manage to create a convincing
  sonic collage of acoustic and electric sounds: jazz swing and hip-hop swa
 g\, and a rollicking funk bottom end. Ultimately\, Persistencestands as a 
 worthy template for a wholly open approach to jazz that's generous enough 
 for the inclusion of myriad influences.
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/amina-figarova-edition-113/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
