BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Another Trip Around the Sun: An Evening of Grateful Dead & Jam Ban
 d Magic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260821T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260821T230000
UID:260726dwRunHwODUOyOwcATepg2g
DESCRIPTION:An Evening of Grateful Dead & Jam Band Magic\n\nFriday\, Augus
 t 21st | Doors 6pm\, Music 6:30pm Sebastopol Community Cultural Center\, 3
 90 Morris St\, Sebastopol\, CA\n\nJoin us for a cosmic celebration of musi
 c and community as Sebastopol Community Cultural Center hosts an unforgett
 able night of Grateful Dead-inspired jams\, featuring an all-star lineup o
 f Bay Area favorites.\n\nAnna Elva brings her dynamic\, pulse-driven drumm
 ing to the stage\, fresh off collaborations with Stu Allen & Mars Hotel an
 d the celebrated 40th Grateful Waltz\, where she shared the stage with som
 e of the scene's brightest stars.\n\nScott Guberman\, acclaimed keyboardis
 t known for his work with Phil Lesh and Friends and his deep\, soulful com
 mand of the Hammond B3\, brings decades of Grateful Dead expertise to ever
 y note he plays.\n\nMark Karan\, the legendary lead guitarist who anchored
  Bob Weir & RatDog for over a decade\, lends his soulful\, blues-infused s
 tyle and unmistakable guitar voodoo to the night's performance.\n\nJP McLe
 an rounds out the rhythm section on bass and vocals\, bringing his steady 
 groove from his work with Melvin Seals & JGB and the broader Northern Cali
 fornia jam scene.\n\nOpening the celebration: Slowstring\, a new folk musi
 c project featuring Sarah Ryan and Jimbo Scott\, adding their own flavor t
 o the night's musical journey.\n\nThis special show is a benefit for the S
 ebastopol Community Cultural Center\, come dance\, donate\, and celebrate 
 community\, music\, and another trip around the sun!
LOCATION:Sebastopol Community Cultural Center
URL:https://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/trip-around-the-sun-concert
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Savor Sonoma - Live Fire & Wine
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260821T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260821T230000
UID:260724nagtQV605EO79XhrZCaJ8w
DESCRIPTION:Taste the very best of wine country. Savor Sonoma is an immers
 ive\, three-day flagship culinary festival. Over one spectacular weekend\,
  you'll explore five distinct experiences alongside national culinary star
 s and celebrated local artisans\, all set against the backdrop of open-fla
 me cooking and world-class Sonoma wines. Ignite your senses across two sp
 ectacular worlds. Step onto the pool deck\, where the rich aroma of live-f
 ire cooking fills the air and chefs plate flame-kissed proteins right befo
 re your eyes. Then\, wander inside to explore a vibrant Sonoma village pou
 ring celebrated local wines\, craft beers\, and agave spirits.\n\nFriday -
  The Headliners' Dinner at AYA:\n\n3:00 - 4:30 p.m. Meet culinary Legend A
 aron Sanchez\n\n6:00 - 7:00 p.m. Welcome cocktails and canapes\n\n7:00 - 1
 1:00 p.m. Five-course collaborative tasting with Aarón Sánchez\, Bryan V
 oltaggio\, Michael Voltaggio\, Charlie Palmer\, and Roy Ellamar\n\nSaturda
 y - Live Fire & Vine:\n\n12:00 - 1:00 p.m. VIP Early Access\n\n1:00 - 5:00
  p.m. General Admission Opens\n\n10:00 p.m. - 1:00 a.m. After Hours at AYA
 \n\nVIP Includes: Early VIP Entry beginning at 12:00 p.m. & an exclusive i
 nvite to AYA's After-Hours Party.\n\nImportant event info:\n\nMust be 21 o
 r over to attend and present valid ID to enter. No refunds\, no exchanges.
LOCATION:Graton Resort & Casino
URL:https://savorsonoma.com/#
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
