UID:260526H4Rv8Xvrx0-ztY-1LsZQ-Q
DESCRIPTION:Dairy Farms & 4-H\, FFA and HFFCF Traditions\n\nGrowing up in 
 Healdsburg has often meant growing up with agriculture\, and that traditio
 n continues today.\n\nElizabeth Bucher\, who grew up on a dairy farm on We
 stside Road\, will tell the story of how her immigrant family established 
 the farm and of the changes in the dairy industry in Sonoma County over th
 e years.\n\nLillie Deas will give a hometown girl’s view of what it mean
 s to grow up in a town that values agricultural education and culture\, wi
 th 4-H and FFA clubs and the annual Future Farmers Country Fair.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza Gazebo
URL:https://www.healdsburgmuseum.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
