BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wilderness First Aid Course
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T170000
UID:260711VQyBCBeue0CLnZZ26vhRbw
DESCRIPTION:First aid training lead by Safety Training Pros\, classes
  are fun with lots of hands-on skills practice. The emphasis is
  on making good decisions by staying calm and safe\, doing a g
 ood patient assessment\, and having good communication and leaders
 hip. \n\nJoin our classes\, where it is safe to learn and OK t
 o make mistakes. Wilderness First Aid is 16 hours (two 8-hour d
 ays) and focuses on practicing skills and covering patient assess
 ment\, shock and bleeding\, head and spinal injuries\, wounds\, m
 usculoskeletal injuries\, and heat and cold illnesses. It also in
 cludes a half-day of outdoor scenario practice of first aid and
  leadership skills. \n\nGain the tools and knowledge to handle a
  wilderness first aid emergency. Registration includes day use fe
 e and class materials. Successful completion of the class include
 s a Wilderness First Aid certificate.\n\nThe instructor will addit
 ionally offer a one-hour CPR/AED course immediately after the Wil
 derness First Aid course. The course will focus on both adults 
 and children and comes with a 2-year certification.\n\nCamping wil
 l be available at the group camp for those who wish to camp o
 n Saturday and Sunday night at no additional cost. Camping might
  also be available Friday night in the general campground area 
 on a first-come\, first-serve basis for an additional $20 per pa
 rticipant.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/summerwfa2026
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sundays in the Plaza: Duo Gadjo (Jazz)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T150000
UID:2607093GSaP2PiKEKsocjPKzO0AA
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a series of relaxing afternoons in the plaza this 
 summer from 1:00 PM - 3:00 PM. Each week will feature a live music perform
 ance from a local band or performer. Not to be confused with Tuesdays in t
 he Plaza\, this is a great opportunity to bring a picnic\, sit back\, rela
 x and enjoy the melodies.\n\nAbout the music: French-born vocalist and gui
 tarist Isabelle Fontaine grew up inspired by Édith Piaf\, Charles Trenet\
 , and Yves Montand\, later building a career across Europe before settling
  in the Bay Area\, where she’s known for her expressive vocals and rhyth
 mic guitar rooted in gypsy swing and American Songbook traditions. San Fra
 ncisco native Jeff Magidson spent two decades in France immersed in blues 
 and jazz\, developing a deep passion for Django Reinhardt’s music\; he i
 s a former member of the Hot Club of San Francisco and an accomplished per
 former\, producer\, and author.\n\nTogether as Duo Gadjo\, they blend thei
 r transatlantic influences into a lively\, vintage-inspired sound—“jaz
 z with a French twist”—featuring gypsy guitars and a repertoire of Fre
 nch classics\, American standards\, and New Orleans blues.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza
URL:https://healdsburg.gov/899/Sundays-in-the-Plaza
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
