DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260828T140000
UID:260610cDOzcG7qpkOwbVoJs8Pgxg
DESCRIPTION:Come visit us at Shone Farm for our Summer U-Pick Fridays!\n\n
 U-Pick Items will include:\n\nStrawberries\n\nBlackberries\n\nRaspberries\
 n\nCut Flowers\n\nPole Beans\n\nHerbs\n\nPeppers\n\nWe will also be sellin
 g cut flowers\, beef\, and value-added goods including olive oil and berry
  preserves. The last two events may also include a produce stand.\n\nWhat 
 to bring:\n\nBring your own basket/container to help us reduce waste! If y
 ou bring wicker\, metal\, or thick plastic\, stop by the cashier before yo
 u head out to the field.\n\nWe recommend wearing sunscreen\, a hat\, and c
 omfortable shoes and bringing a water bottle.\n\nEvent details:\n\nOpen to
  the public\n\nKid & family friendly\n\nCard and tap-to-pay accepted\n\nFr
 ee parking and admission\n\nNo reservation needed\n\nMeet our students and
  see them in action!\n\nNo dogs permitted\, except assistance dogs
LOCATION:Shone Farm
URL:https://shonefarm.santarosa.edu/summer-u-pick
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Music & Memories - Providence Community Health Foundation Annual G
 ala
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260828T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260828T213000
UID:260521x5-n0O_HuUSBdT7hr0DOvw
DESCRIPTION:Join us on August 28th for an evening where each beat\, song\,
  and memory will make a difference!\n\nThrough Music and Memories\, we're 
 raising essential funds to provide care and encouragement for those in our
  community dealing with Alzheimer's or dementia\, and support for those wh
 o love them.\n\nOur 20th annual celebration will be one of the highlights 
 of the fall social season in the Napa Valley and offers an experience to r
 emember. The event will feature a fun wine reception\, a live band\, and a
  delicious dinner\, followed by a “fund-a-need."\n\nHere are some critic
 al projects your generosity will make possible:\n\nFamily consultations - 
 ensuring everyone gets the help they need\n\nCaregiver support groups - of
 fering a shoulder to lean on\n\nCommunity workshops and education - spread
 ing knowledge and resources\n\nRespite care – providing caregivers a muc
 h-needed break\n\nYour support doesn’t just fund programs—it brings co
 mfort\, dignity\, and connection to those facing one of life’s most diff
 icult journeys. Together\, we are building a more compassionate\, informed
 \, and resilient community.\n\nHonorary Chair: Violet Grgich\; Culinary Ho
 st: Chef Ken Frank of La Toque
LOCATION:Grgich Hills Estates
URL:https://musicandmemoriesnapa.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sacred Sound Sessions: Mantra Love & Lullaby — Jai Uttal with Ma
 nose
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260828T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260828T210000
UID:260430vI-zKmP8UE-NUTODyDThgg
DESCRIPTION:Spirit Rock invites you to experience our annual Sacred Sounds
  concert series! Each session will feature a musical artist devoted to cre
 ating\, honoring\, and sharing sacred spiritual music in many exciting for
 ms. Join us for a nourishing and uplifting combination of transformative m
 usic in our Great Hall\, an optional bring-your-own picnic outside in natu
 re\, and an opportunity to gather with saṅgha on our stunning Spirit Roc
 k land. Gates will open two hours before the performance.\n\nFor six decad
 es\, Jai Uttal has walked the path of the mystical art and deep practice o
 f sacred sound. Since his youth\, Jai’s musical journey has carried him 
 to every corner of the world\, and what he has distilled from these decade
 s of study and experience is\, quite simply\, the essence of devotion. His
  music serves as a bridge between the ancient traditions of kirtan and the
  contemporary heart\, offering a space where practice and melody become on
 e.\n\nWe invite you to come and bathe in the “sonic balm” of Jai’s v
 oice\, songs\, and instruments. In this space of sanctuary\, we will raise
  our voices together to inspire and open the heart\, culminating in a gent
 ly soothing lullaby of mantra\, melody\, and love. Jai will be joined by w
 orld-renowned Nepalese bansuri player Manose\, whose exquisite flute work 
 transports the listener to heavenly realms\, deepening the container of pe
 ace and presence.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/sacred-sound-sessions-
 mantra-love-lullaby-jai-uttal-with-manose-ja1e26/?lang=en
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
